post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
This package installs the nvim-mcp server binary.

The Neovim plugin is optional. It creates one socket per project so that 
nvim-mcp --connect auto finds the running instance. In neovim, you would
add this to your init.lua:

  vim.pack.add({
    { name = 'nvim-mcp', src = 'https://github.com/linw1995/nvim-mcp' },
  })
  require('nvim-mcp').setup({})

If you don't use the plugin, just make sure you start Neovim with a socket
that matches the glob nvim-mcp knows to search for:

  nvim --listen "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nvim-mcp-shared.sock"

Registering the server with various agent harnesses:

  # claude
  claude mcp add --scope user Neovim -- nvim-mcp

  # codex
  codex mcp add Neovim -- nvim-mcp

  # opencode
  opencode mcp add --global Neovim -- nvim-mcp

EOF
}
